  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the Casualty Card NEWS2 engine. calculateNEWS2 returns totalScore, seven parameterScores in fixed order (Respiratory Rate, SpO2 (Scale 1), Systolic BP, Pulse, Consciousness, Temperature, Supplemental O2), hasAnySingleScore3 and clinicalResponse ('high' >= 7, 'medium' >= 5, 'low-medium' when any single parameter scores 3, else 'low'). Flags are SPLIT: form-app.js calls detectFlaggedIssues(state, news2), mirrored as flagsArgs ['state','result']; the oracle stores them under expected.flaggedIssues. HARNESS CAVEAT: form-app.js calls calculateNEWS2(state.vitalSigns) - a SUB-OBJECT - but bin/test-personas has no graderArgs and always passes the whole persona state, under which every vital would read as undefined and score 0. So each persona's state carries the full emptyCasualtyCard() shape (which the detector reads: safeguardingConsent, medicalHistory, primarySurvey, vitalSigns.pupil*, investigations) PLUS the seven scored vital keys (respiratoryRate, oxygenSaturation, systolicBP, heartRate, consciousnessLevel, temperature, supplementalOxygen) mirrored at the top level, kept identical to vitalSigns, so the grader scores the same numbers the UI would. Quirks verified in source: any unmeasured parameter (null) scores 0 with value 'N/A' rather than being flagged; SpO2 is always Scale 1 (no hypercapnic Scale 2); consciousnessLevel '' scores 0 like 'alert' while any other string scores 3; boundaries are inclusive on the upper edge of each band (temp 35.0 -> 3, HR 50 -> 1, SpO2 91 -> 3, SBP 90 -> 3); the 'haemorrhage' flag fires for ANY non-empty text other than exactly 'none' (case-insensitive), so an explicit negative like 'None visible' fires it; the 'mha-section' flag fires for ANY non-empty mentalHealthActStatus including 'Informal'; the anticoagulant check is a substring match over a fixed seven-drug list; gcsTotal is read from state (recomputeDerived() is a form-app.js step the oracle does not run) so personas set it consistently with the components; news2-critical and news2-medium are mutually exclusive and both priority 'high'; the priority sort is stable so flags keep detection order within a priority. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas casualty-card-form --update",
